    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0771" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Lieutenant General Alvan C. Gillem,
                        Jr. </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">OSE 466</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-09-27">27 September
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Marshall desires that all action to complete the so-called reoccupation
                    (of Manchuria) program, that is the supply of ammunition and combat equipment to
                    the Chinese Government, be deferred until further notice from him.</p>
                <closer>For General Marshall: <lb/>
                    <signed>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hart Caughey</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Colonel, G. S. C.</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
